/target
Cargo.lock.bak
**/*.rs.bk
*.swp
# .DS_Store

# Test/playwright ephemeral artifacts
.meta-snapshots/
# .playwright-mcp/
scripts/__pycache__/

# Agent harness output (generated, not committed)
# .agent/
.archive/

# envctl.lock IS committed — it is the content-hashed manifest-of-record and the
# baseline for `envctl lock --check` (the CI drift gate). Do not ignore it.

# GitKB — track the durable TEXT store (documents/commits/refs/manifest.json =
# the source of truth) so the KB survives clone/reclaim and travels in git.
# Ignore ONLY the rebuildable index cache (`git-kb reindex` regenerates .cache
# from store) and the ephemeral editing surfaces. Mirrors the `.handoff` rule
# above (track text; never commit binary rebuild caches).
#   NOTE: `git-kb init`'s tool default ignores `.kb/store/` wholesale — that is
#   WRONG here: it makes the KB non-durable (nothing committed/pushed; the docs
#   are lost on a fresh clone). See META-ORG-POLICY (.kb store-durability rule).
.kb/.cache/
.kb/workspace/
.kb/workspaces/
.kb/store/stashes/

# === handoff continuity kernel — canonical .handoff durability policy (ADR-0016 / ADR-0018 D1) ===
# REGENERABLE .handoff state — the LOCAL rebuild cache (the binary ledger is re-derived from the
# committed `.handoff/ledger.events.jsonl` via `hf import`) + ephemeral runtime + out-of-tree
# migration artifacts: never commit. The committed continuity truth is the JSONL export and the
# rendered views (packets/, active.md, deliveries/) — those are DURABLE and intentionally absent
# here so they stay committed (ADR-0018 D1).
# CONTENTS-FORM only — NEVER a bare `.handoff/` or `.claude/` ignore: Git cannot re-include a
# path past an excluded parent dir, so a dir-form ignore silently SWALLOWS durable ledgers
# (tasks/, decisions/, loop/*.md). Run `hf gitignore --check` (or `hf doctor`) to detect it.
.handoff/**/ledger.db
.handoff/**/*.db-wal
.handoff/**/*.db-shm
.handoff/**/*.rvf
.handoff/**/*.rvf.lock
.handoff/**/*.sqlite.bak
.handoff/**/*.redb.tmp
/.handoff/workspaces/
/.handoff/locks/
/.handoff/maps/
